Date: Sat, 6 Jun 2026 14:16:51 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] perf: fully async actor-model waypoint manager

Move all locator-bar work off the tick thread. A single dedicated worker
owns the connection table and the waypoint/player sets; every mutating op
is enqueued onto it, so the non-thread-safe HashBasedTable is touched by
one thread without locking. The tick thread only marks dirty (O(1)) and
once per tick dispatches a batch.

The only state unsafe to read off-thread - each receiver's sent-chunk set
(getSentChunksRaw, used by isChunkVisible) - is cloned on the tick thread
into a per-batch snapshot published to the worker via a ThreadLocal and
consulted there instead of the live set. The clone is wrapped defensively
so a rare off-thread lifecycle call degrades to a flicker, never a crash.
Positions/attributes are read live off-thread (no crashing structures),
like the async entity tracker.

- ServerWaypointManager: actor model, snapshot capture/publish, batching
- WaypointTransmitter.isChunkVisible: use the snapshot when on the worker

