+/**
+ * Fully asynchronous, actor-model waypoint (locator bar) manager.
+ *
+ * <p>All waypoint state - the non-thread-safe {@code connections} table plus the waypoint/player sets -
+ * is owned by a single dedicated worker thread ({@link #WAYPOINT_EXECUTOR}). Every mutating operation is
+ * enqueued onto that thread, so the table is only ever touched by one thread and never needs locking.
+ * Packet sends are thread-safe (Netty), so they happen on the worker too. The server tick thread only
+ * does O(1) work: it marks moved entities dirty and once per tick enqueues a single batch.
+ *
+ * <p>The one piece of state the worker needs that is NOT safe to read off-thread is each receiver's set
+ * of sent chunks ({@code getSentChunksRaw()}, used by {@link WaypointTransmitter#isChunkVisible}). That
+ * set is cloned on the TICK thread (where the read is safe) into a per-batch snapshot, published to the
+ * worker via {@link #SENT_SNAPSHOT}, and consulted there instead of the live set. Entity positions are
+ * read live off-thread (immutable Vec3 refs), which is tolerable - only the fastutil set would crash.
+ */
